# Practical AI for TPMs

When the user invokes a `/tpm-*` slash command, read the mapped file from root `CLAUDE.md` and follow it exactly.

## Always load first

- `2-goals-policies/domain-context.md`
- `2-goals-policies/personal-context.md`

## Program Architect (9-agent suite)

Full workflow: `/tpm-workflow-program-architect` → `5-agent-harness/workflows/tpm-workflow-program-architect.md`

Standalone agents in `5-agent-harness/sub-agents/`:

| Command | File |
|---------|------|
| `/tpm-ops-framework` | `tpm-ops-framework.md` |
| `/tpm-scope-cutter` | `tpm-scope-cutter.md` |
| `/tpm-build-vs-buy` | `tpm-build-vs-buy.md` |
| `/tpm-effort-estimator` | `tpm-effort-estimator.md` |
| `/tpm-quarter-architect` | `tpm-quarter-architect.md` |
| `/tpm-program-roadmap` | `tpm-program-roadmap.md` |
| `/tpm-platform-decision` | `tpm-platform-decision.md` |
| `/tpm-ai-validator` | `tpm-ai-validator.md` |
| `/tpm-launch-auditor` | `tpm-launch-auditor.md` |

**Human checkpoint:** After Stage 4 (scope + estimates), stop and get explicit TPM sign-off before roadmap stages.

